# Talaria JavaScript SDK

npm workspaces. Published packages: `@newtalaria/browser`, `@newtalaria/core`, `@newtalaria/node`, `@newtalaria/react`, `@newtalaria/nextjs`.

## Role

```
App → Talaria.init
        ├─ capture* / logger     → POST /v1/events
        ├─ Tracer (optional APM) → POST /v1/spans
        └─ analytics.* (opt-in)  → POST /v1/analytics
Browser only: rrweb → POST /v1/replays, /v1/replays/segments, /v1/replays/{id}/finish
```

- Fingerprinting is **server-side only**
- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer` with a `tal_pk_` (browser) or `tal_sk_` (server) key
- Always batch ingest
- Never wrap `ServerpodTransport` with tracing middleware
- Tracing off until `enableTracing` / `tracesSampleRate`
- Browser pageload / navigation roots are idle spans — see `tracing.mdc`

## Package map

| Path | npm | Role |
| ---- | --- | ---- |
| `packages/core/` | `@newtalaria/core` | Isomorphic types, transport, sampling, scope |
| `packages/browser/` | `@newtalaria/browser` | DOM, replay, fetch/XHR, vitals, History |
| `packages/node/` | `@newtalaria/node` | Process + HTTP in/out |
| `packages/react/` | `@newtalaria/react` | ErrorBoundary, Profiler, React Router |
| `packages/nextjs/` | `@newtalaria/nextjs` | Client / server / edge / config |

## Explicit don'ts

- Do not import `react` or `next` from `packages/core`
- Do not import Node `http` from `packages/browser` or `packages/react`
- Do not pull `@newtalaria/node` into `@newtalaria/nextjs/client`
- Do not compute fingerprints
- Always batch ingest (`POST /v1/events` takes `{ events: [...] }`)

## Fail safe (Talaria workspace D19)

Decided by Heath (2026-11-03): "having an invalid Talaria key shouldnt stop the site from building. It should just stop Talaria working". That is the default for every SDK. Full rule: `.cursor/skills/sdk-fail-safe/SKILL.md` in `dunatron/talaria-workspace`.

- Init never throws. A missing, empty, malformed, wrong-checksum or revoked key, or any bad init option, builds a disabled no-op client. Every public method returns normally and sends nothing.
- Log one warning per process, showing at most the key's first 8 characters.
- Keep the key grammar strict. A parse failure disables Talaria. It is never an exception the host app sees.
- Transport errors (4xx, 5xx, timeouts, DNS, TLS) never reach host code. Log them rate-limited.
- Framework hooks (factories, providers, middleware, log handlers, error hooks) catch their own Talaria errors, so a Talaria fault never becomes a 500 or a crash.
- Builds and install steps never fail because of Talaria.
- Tests: no key, empty key, malformed key, wrong checksum and bad option each give no throw, a no-op client and one warning. Transport 401, 500 and timeout never reach the caller.
- Code: `packages/core/src/fail_safe.ts` (`warnDisabledOnce`, `logRateLimited`, `keyPreview`). Each `init` catches the throwing credential helpers and calls `warnDisabledOnce`. `isEnabled()` is false when disabled. Tests live in each package's `test/fail_safe.test.ts`.
- `talaria source-maps upload` and `talaria-nextjs upload` exit 0 with a warning on a missing or bad key, an unreachable Talaria or a failed upload. Only a usage error exits non-zero.
